Filetype: IR library file
Version: 1
#
# GURU bundled television codes (#187).
#
# WHERE THESE COME FROM. Every entry is a verbatim record from the Flipper Zero IR
# library's tv asset, the actively maintained community database. Nothing here was
# invented or hand-tuned: a synthesised code that is close but wrong presses nothing,
# and a code that looks plausible is worse than no code because it sends you looking
# in the wrong place.
#
# HOW THE FILE IS GROUPED. Each '# Model:' or model-name comment starts a device and
# every block beneath it belongs to that device. The attribution is load-bearing: a
# power button from one make is silence on another, so a code filed under the wrong
# model is a wrong code.
#
# WHY ONLY MAKES WITH A POWER BUTTON. A remote set with no power code cannot switch a
# television on, so it is not a controllable device and listing it would offer a
# device whose only useful command always refuses. Every make below has at least a
# working power button.
#
# VOLUME NEEDS BOTH DIRECTIONS. A set with only volume down cannot turn anything up,
# so VOLUME is offered only where volume up exists. A make with one direction keeps
# the other buttons and simply does not claim the capability it cannot perform.
#
# RAW ENTRIES ARE KEPT AS THEY ARE. Some makes record a button as a capture rather
# than a named protocol, and a capture is transmitted exactly as recorded.

